course: dictionary
lesson: 8868
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. Read this: «Time feels shorter when you are playing and longer when you are waiting.» Here short is about time: it means lasting only a little while.
explain: Now read: «Shorts are short trousers.» The first short is the name of the clothes, and the second short describes their length. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Short can also describe height, as in a short person, or having too little, as in «run short of milk». A dictionary lists all the meanings, but the sentence shows you which one to choose.
fact: Short means not long, as in a short pencil or a short story.
fact: Short means not tall, as in a short person.
fact: Short means lasting a little time, as in «a short break».
fact: Short of something means not having enough of it, so «$4 short» means you need $4 more.
fact: «Short for» means a shorter form of a name: Tom is short for Thomas.
exercise: In «a short break», what does short mean? | Not having enough | *Lasting a little time | Not tall | Shorts, the trousers
exercise: In «Tom is short for Thomas», what does short for mean? | Lasting a little time | *A shorter form of a name | Not tall | Not having enough
exercise: Sam has $1 and the bike costs $5. Which phrase describes Sam? | Short for a name | A short story | *Short of money | Short trousers
test: In «a short explanation of what a word means», what does short mean? | *Not long | Lasting a little time | Not tall | Not having enough
test: «The shop had run short of milk.» What does run short of mean? | Had lots of milk | Ran very fast | *Did not have enough milk | Was closed for a short time
exam: In «Shorts are short trousers», what does the second short mean? | Not tall | Lasting a little time | Not having enough | *Not long
